{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent negative bias: model forecasts are systematically below realized prices across most horizons (often by ~2–5 EUR), especially during uptrends; apply an upward level shift.",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the last 1–2 weeks show a rising regime, the model fails to propagate the trend and reverts too quickly; add a positive trend term proportional to recent slope (e.g., 10–20d momentum).",
    "Horizon-dependent drift: underprediction tends to grow with forecast horizon (errors widen after ~day 7–10); use a horizon-scaling uplift that increases with lead time.",
    "Upside spikes not captured: during breakout/rally phases the model caps too low and misses higher highs; include a regime switch that increases uplift when price breaks above recent 20–30d range/MA.",
    "Occasional late-horizon overshoot down: some forecasts dip sharply lower in the final third despite continued strength; constrain late-horizon mean reversion unless recent volatility is accompanied by confirmed reversal signals."
  ]
}
